  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trauma Programme-Avega National</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It is an association of genocide widows created in 1995, in partnership with CAFOD since 1996. It aims to promote the integration of the widows and strengthen their self-promotion and participation in the process of development in Rwanda.

As part of the 3 years psychosocial programme, the AVEGA project in 2008 is mainly training and supervision of psychosocial animators, individual and group counselling. AVEGA will be conducting activities aiming at the social integration of the population affected by trauma, social cohesion and reconciliation through community based approaches. The programme also contains other activities aiming at reducing the vulnerability of women and children mostly orphans with the objective of increasing access to justice. 

The main activities planned in 2008 are: assistance in school materials to 450 children, 20 houses rehabilitation, training of 120 new paralegals and refresher course for 220 Psychosocial Animators, 2600 clinical supervisions for APS, training in stepping stones for communities, special assistance in basic needs for 300 widows and orphans, special medical care for 10 widows and funeral assistance to 20 households. AVEGA will receive funds for overheads administrative and capital costs. Counselling sessions are planned all the period of the year and are due to be done by both Trauma counsellors and Psychosocial Animators (APS).</narrative>
  </description>
